    @PreAuthorize("isAuthenticated()")
    public ResponseEntity<Void> vote(
            @PathVariable Long id,
            @RequestBody VoteDTO dto,
            @AuthenticationPrincipal UserDetails userDetails) {
        
        User user = userService.findByEmail(userDetails.getUsername());
        service.recordVote(id, dto.questionId, dto.answerIndex, user.getId());
        
        return ResponseEntity.noContent().build();
    }
    
    @GetMapping("/{id}/results")
    public ResponseEntity<SondageResultsDTO> getResults(@PathVariable Long id) {
        return ResponseEntity.ok(service.getResults(id));
    }
}
```

### Key Design Decisions

**1. Why separate Vote entity?**
- Track who voted and when
- Prevent duplicate votes
- Audit trail for integrity

**2. Why ElementCollection for answers?**
- Simple data structure
- No need for separate table
- Easier to query

**3. Why aggregate counts in service?**
- Complex calculation
- Not suitable for database query
- Reusable across endpoints

**4. Why FormArray?**
- Dynamic question/answer fields
- Easy to add/remove
- Programmatic form building

